## Modern Patterns to Use

- Signal-based reactive programming
- Standalone components with explicit imports
- Function-based dependency injection (`inject()`)
- Native control flow in templates (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`)
- Resource API for streaming data
- Error boundaries for RSS parsing failures
- Progressive Web App features for offline reading

## Patterns to Avoid

- Module-based architecture (use standalone)
- Constructor-based dependency injection
- Structural directives (`*ngIf`, `*ngFor`, `*ngSwitch`)
- `ngClass` and `ngStyle`
- Complex template expressions
- Direct DOM manipulation
- Using `any` type

